MT-B14 (review R6): a Monero lock that cannot be spent until later opens no gate — real regtest monerod and
monero-wallet-rpc 0.18.5.1, and the DERO simulator
==============================================================================================================
Run 2026-09-12 from 12:23 AEST: tools/simhtlc -regtest -paths unlock, built with go1.26.8 from the working tree. The
raw driver output follows this header; machine paths are written <tmp>, <repo> and <user>.

The rule, as monero 0.18.5.1 states it (the source at tag v0.18.5.1)
- cryptonote_config.h:49  CRYPTONOTE_DEFAULT_TX_SPENDABLE_AGE 10: an output is spendable 10 blocks after the block it
  is in.
- cryptonote_config.h:40  CRYPTONOTE_MAX_BLOCK_NUMBER 500000000: an unlock_time below it is a block height, above it a
  unix time.
- cryptonote_config.h:44  CRYPTONOTE_MINED_MONEY_UNLOCK_WINDOW 60: a coinbase carries unlock_time = its height + 60.
- cryptonote_config.h:90  CRYPTONOTE_LOCKED_TX_ALLOWED_DELTA_BLOCKS 1.
- wallet2.cpp:7308-7317   is_transfer_unlocked: an output is unlocked only when is_tx_spendtime_unlocked passes AND
  block_height + CRYPTONOTE_DEFAULT_TX_SPENDABLE_AGE <= the chain height.
- wallet2.cpp:7319-7344   is_tx_spendtime_unlocked: a height unlock_time passes when chain height − 1 +
  CRYPTONOTE_LOCKED_TX_ALLOWED_DELTA_BLOCKS >= unlock_time; a time one when the daemon's adjusted time plus a leeway
  reaches it.
- wallet_rpc_server.cpp:498, 517  get_transfers reports each transfer's "locked" = !is_transfer_unlocked(unlock_time,
  block_height), and its "unlock_time"; wallet_rpc_server.cpp:501 marks a coinbase with type "block", in the same "in"
  list as any other payment.
- wallet2.cpp:7826        a 0.18.5.1 wallet refuses to build a transaction with any unlock_time
  (error::nonzero_unlock_time); wallet_rpc_server.cpp:1250, 1310, 1763, 1829 turn that into the RPC's -50
  "Transaction cannot have non-zero unlock time".

Why the lock here is a coinbase
  monero-wallet-rpc 0.18.5.1 will not build a transfer with an unlock_time, far future or near. Measured on this
  regtest wallet-rpc (alice's, with do_not_relay, nothing broadcast), 2026-09-12:
    transfer, unlock_time 1000000  ->  -50 "Transaction cannot have non-zero unlock time"
    transfer, unlock_time 7000     ->  -50 "Transaction cannot have non-zero unlock time"
  So no honest taker's companion can make such a lock, and none can be "crafted" through the wallet-rpc. The one
  locked output that can reach an address on regtest is a coinbase: mining a block to the joint address gives it an
  output of the whole block reward with unlock_time = the block's height + 60. The driver does that in place of
  alice's transfer (tools/simhtlc coinbaseLock); everything else — bob's view wallet, the gate, the refund, alice's
  recovery sweep — is the companions' own code against the real servers. On mainnet the same output arises when a
  miner, or a pool acting for the taker, pays a coinbase to the joint address, or when another program builds a
  transaction with an unlock_time.

What the companion does with it (tools/xmrswap/swap.go confirmedAtJoint)
  Bob's gate counts no transfer whose unlock_time is not 0, whatever its value, and never more than the wallet's
  unlocked balance. The wallet's own "locked" flag and that cap already keep out an output that is still locked when
  he counts; the explicit rule also keeps out one whose lock has passed, and makes him say why.

Driver policy (not the companion's defaults): t1 = lock + 48 DERO blocks, t2 = t1 + 8, G = 4, bob's depth 10 Monero
confirmations, one regtest block mined per driver round, a 60-minute limit on the path. The DERO side is the
simulator; nothing here is testnet or mainnet.

Command (from <repo>/tools, built to simhtlc_unlock.exe):
  simhtlc -regtest -paths unlock -timeout 60m -prover "wsl.exe -e <path to the reproducible proof-xmr build>"
          -state-dir <tmp>/e2estate_unlock
Pre-run check (first line of the raw output): no transfer on DERO wallets 30006 or 30007 since height 338, no other
simhtlc or xmrswap process, an empty monerod pool.

