  Nothing of this run is left running. No wake task was registered: simhtlc runs the companions without an OS wake
  hook, and alice's card said so ("wake: none registered"); the Task Scheduler holds no xmrswap task.

What it shows, and what it does not
  - A lock that cannot be spent until later — here 60 blocks — opens no gate, on the real wallet-rpc: bob refused it
    from the first sight until t1, the whole time it was still locked, and refunded at t1; alice ended with the output,
    not with a loss. That is review R6's case: the gate is never released against coins neither side can move in time.
  - A far-future unlock_time on a non-coinbase transaction was not made here, because monero-wallet-rpc 0.18.5.1
    cannot build one (the -50 above). The fake-wallet test covers that case, a far-future height and a far-future time
    (tools/xmrswap/unlock_test.go TestAFarLockedOutputOpensNoGate); the code path bob takes is the same, keyed on the
    unlock_time get_transfers reports.

